Assistance is provided in line with cluster (WASH, Shelter & NFI) standards and beneficiaries are selected based upon agreed vulnerability criteria:
-	Female Headed Household; 
-	Child Headed Household; 
-	Disabled Headed Household; 
-	Elderly Headed Household with no adults having an income; 
-	Households with children under 5 with Severe Acute Malnutrition (SAM) or Moderate Acute Malnutrition (MAM);
-	Vulnerable Households with children under five years old and/or pregnant women and/or lactating women;
-	Very Large Family (8 members or more) with only one adult having an income; 
-	Very Poor Families; 
-	Families with Chronically-ill or disabled members or having other pressing vulnerability.

To achieve the goal of Yemeni women having greater influence in fostering durable peace and inclusive public decision-making at local and sub-national levels, CARE is proposing a three-pronged approach: 
1.	Provide capacity-building for Yemeni CSOs and Yemeni women’s groups working on grassroots peacebuilding; and 
2.	Promote gender equality amongst Yemeni youth groups and support them to engage in advocacy and their communities; and 
3.	Promote gender equality amongst influential men. 

Overarching ToC: 
IF CSOs and women’s groups have enhanced knowledge and capacities and have gained opportunities in decision-making and peacebuilding; which are supported with resources, actionable learning and spaces to collaboratively address drivers of local conflict and inequality;
AND Youth groups have enhanced capacities and knowledge in gender equality, decision-making, and peacebuilding and linkages with CSO’s and women’s groups; with the understanding they are the future leaders and decision-makers;
AND Decision-makers have embraced and contributed to an enabling environment for peacebuilding and inclusive gender norms, thereby supporting youth and women’s participation in decision-making; 
THEN Women and youth will influence local peacebuilding initiatives and participate in inclusive decision-making, a proven contributor to durable peace.
